{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics","id":1367763,"title":"On demon summoning and ethics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-14T08:13:03-08:00","id":1367763,"title":"On demon summoning and ethics","content":"Look, I know its probably done to death, and you all already thought of this...<br /> <br /> But has anyone thought of Demon-summoning? I mean, you are grabbing a creature, taking it from its home, and then binding it to your will to do whatever you want. From sex, to dying against an enemy, or labour. You're applying mind control to it to do stuff for you. Potentially forever. <br /> <br /> I mean, there's stuff about how life in Creation is a lot more nicer than Malfeas, but that sounds like a lot of the apologism for slavery. <br /> <br /> This applies for elementals as well. There's a lot of debate on the ethics of creating an A.I. or designer babies for an explicit purpose. Think what comes up when you summon an elemental for, say, giving yourself a cold breeze or starting fires. <br /> <br /> So the question is, is in the face of modern ethics, is it in any way defensible to summon, and bind, demons and elementals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:25:55-08:00","id":1367769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics#post1367763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I know its probably done to death, and you all already thought of this...<br /> <br /> But has anyone thought of Demon-summoning? I mean, you are grabbing a creature, taking it from its home, and then binding it to your will to do whatever you want. From sex, to dying against an enemy, or labour. You're applying mind control to it to do stuff for you. Potentially forever.<br /> <br /> I mean, there's stuff about how life in Creation is a lot more nicer than Malfeas, but that sounds like a lot of the apologism for slavery.<br /> <br /> This applies for elementals as well. There's a lot of debate on the ethics of creating an A.I. or designer babies for an explicit purpose. Think what comes up when you summon an elemental for, say, giving yourself a cold breeze or starting fires.<br /> <br /> So the question is, is in the face of modern ethics, is it in any way defensible to summon, and bind, demons and elementals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the first logical answer is &quot;You can't defend it&quot;, but you can treat them well. For example, the elementals you create do not exist before (if I remember well), so you basically create a sort of conscience and allows for it to develop. If you don't treat it poorly, I don't see this any differently than adopting an animal (I guess there can be discussions about specific parts of animal rights and should human interact with animals at all but I won't go on this complicated topic) and treating it well.<br /> <br /> For demons I guess it's different. I don't really have an idea about this, because they have needs and desires far too different from us to understand, but I guess on first approximation, if they are not unhappy with what you are asking them to do, it's not too bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:26:48-08:00","id":1367770,"title":"","content":"What is modern ethics?<br /> <br /> Is a lion morally wrong to eat a human?<br /> Is a human morally wrong to kill a lion trying to eat it?<br /> <br /> Rothbard has a chapter in The Ethics of Liberty stating it is not morally wrong to for humans to kill alien space vampires (no, really -- studying ethics is great RPG material). I think his arguments apply to Exalted summoning demons.<br /> <br /> Longer reply later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367769#post1367769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the elementals you create do not exist before (if I remember well), so you basically create a sort of conscience and allows for it to develop. If you don't treat it poorly, I don't see this any differently than adopting an animal</div> </div> </div> </div>Or having a child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:32:05-08:00","id":1367771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics#post1367763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But has anyone thought of Demon-summoning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics#post1367763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you are grabbing a creature, taking it from its home, and then binding it to your will to do whatever you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though to be fair, a <i>smart</i> demon summoner will summon a demon to do something <i>the demon</i> wants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics#post1367763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From sex, to dying against an enemy, or labour. You're applying mind control to it to do stuff for you. Potentially forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But here's the thing: if it wanted to do that stuff anyway, then all you've really done is given it a free ticket to Creation and asked it to do that on your behalf specifically. Heck, you can even pay the demon for its labor; the spell isn't stopping you from doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics#post1367763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there's stuff about how life in Creation is a lot more nicer than Malfeas, but that sounds like a lot of the apologism for slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in the wrong hands, demon summoning is absolutely slavery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics#post1367763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think what comes up when you summon an elemental for, say, giving yourself a cold breeze or starting fires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why something so small? Do you feel like that's what most sorcerers who summon elementals will task them to do?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics#post1367763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the question is, is in the face of modern ethics, is it in any way defensible to summon, and bind, demons and elementals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Contact them ahead of time, bargain with them for their service, and after you summon them, pay them for their work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-14-2020, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:35:30-08:00","id":1367772,"title":"","content":"Most summoners, to my understanding, don\u2019t object to the characterization of binding sentient if alien life forms to serve them. Iirc, blood apes find Creation unpleasant. <br /> Ethical defenses of enslaving demons probably hinge on demons not being human and thus fundamentally different things ethically, more than anything abou creation being nicer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:41:02-08:00","id":1367774,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> You can contact a demon without using the spell to summon them ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:44:13-08:00","id":1367776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367774#post1367774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> You can contact a demon without using the spell to summon them ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, there might be problems. <br /> <br /> Teodizja might ask for converts. Firmin might ask for people to impale. Puppeteers might ask for babies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:45:53-08:00","id":1367777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367774#post1367774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> You can contact a demon without using the spell to summon them ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while the Infallible Messenger spell won't cross interplanar boundaries, the fact is that demons <i>do</i> reside in the Demon City when they're not summoned, and beings <i>can</i> travel to and from the Demon City; passing along a message to a hellbound demon to seek out other demons for employment under you is plausible. Hell, you could even (very carefully!) open a portal via a Working and throw employment pamphlets through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:48:28-08:00","id":1367778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367776#post1367776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, there might be problems.<br /> <br /> Teodizja might ask for converts. Firmin might ask for people to impale. Puppeteers might ask for babies.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if their asking price is something that you're not willing to pay, <i>you don't hire them</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T09:00:42-08:00","id":1367783,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> I like your answers, but it demands of the player and ST to handle demon summoning very differently from what I've seen in my games so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T09:20:27-08:00","id":1367789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367783#post1367783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> I like your answers, but it demands of the player and ST to handle demon summoning very differently from what I've seen in my games so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Lots of the actions of player characters are not necessarily going to conform to what's considered by a modern person to be reasonable or ethical/moral behavior.<br /> <br /> \u200bMost sorcerers aren't going to bother with contacting demons ahead of time to bargain with them for their services and then pay them a hefty sum. They're going to use them as slave labor because it's convenient. If they even have qualms about slavery they probably won't care as much about demons being subjected to it because demons aren't humans, and generally possess less capacity to object to their mistreatment to the sorcerer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-14-2020, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T09:28:21-08:00","id":1367790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367777#post1367777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, while the Infallible Messenger spell won't cross interplanar boundaries, the fact is that demons <i>do</i> reside in the Demon City when they're not summoned, and beings <i>can</i> travel to and from the Demon City; passing along a message to a hellbound demon to seek out other demons for employment under you is plausible. Hell, you could even (very carefully!) open a portal via a Working and throw employment pamphlets through.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm now imagining weekly demon job fairs during the First Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T09:40:42-08:00","id":1367793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367790#post1367790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm now imagining weekly demon job fairs during the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Remember fellows blood apes, what interests recrutors nowadays are transversal competences and soft skills. Try to think of how you can use your blade-like claws in situations that prove you are able to manage a team. Your only limit is your imagination and dedication !&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T09:47:52-08:00","id":1367796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics#post1367763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But has anyone thought of Demon-summoning? I mean, you are grabbing a creature, taking it from its home, and then binding it to your will to do whatever you want. From sex, to dying against an enemy, or labour. You're applying mind control to it to do stuff for you. Potentially forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a tad more nuance to it then that. But sure, it does amount to a largely one way exploitative power dynamic (although that gap gets narrower as you go down the circles; it can be a tad perilous to summon the unquestionable).<br /> <br /> As how to characterize the interaction goes, I feel as though among First Circle Demons who even have consciousness their personal liberty isn't quite the highest on their list of priorities, because they don't exactly have it anyway. And considering the point of summoning, you're probably bringing them in to do the kind of thing they live for anyway. I think it's valid to portray blood apes as not being upset to maim and feed on behalf of another rather than themselves. What were you even summoning them for otherwise. Hell, the agatae thrive on being steeds for others (and their magically bound Intimacies don't necessarily stop them from having fits of emotion that cause them to buck their riders off).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This applies for elementals as well. There's a lot of debate on the ethics of creating an A.I. or designer babies for an explicit purpose. Think what comes up when you summon an elemental for, say, giving yourself a cold breeze or starting fires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that what comes up when you summon something for that purpose might have the intelligence of an insect or a fish.<br /> <br /> I'm against going out of one's way to kill mayflies, but don't quite mourn that they have such short lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">in the face of modern ethics, is it in any way defensible to summon, and bind, demons and elementals?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the summoning of spirits was a thing that definitively existed in reality, ethical arguments against doing so on grounds of the agency of those spirits would probably exist.<br /> <br /> But I think the subject is far enough removed from reality that it shouldn't present much of a challenge for people to play the role of characters who are unconcerned with it, even if they are with things like clear cut human slavery.<br /> <br /> Heck, I feel there are greater ethical considerations to bringing steeds or familiars into combat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T10:21:40-08:00","id":1367804,"title":"","content":"Sorcery taps into the surrender paths of the Yozi right? You could make a case that summoning and binding demons is then just fulfilling the terms of their surrender to the army of the gods.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, no I don\u2019t really see a defensible position of demon summoning as a moral thing to just be doing. On the other hand we are taking about demonologists summoning forth inhuman monsters from Hell and directing their baleful intelligence towards something in Creation. Should we be framing this in a moral way? Nothing else about it seems to imply that it\u2019s a nice thing to be doing. Not that you shouldn\u2019t be one. Both this edition\u2019s signature Exalts and the previous one\u2019s have had some pretty serious moral failings themselves. The world of Creation is like Game of Thrones or the Witcher or something. The TV tropes would be a Crapsack world with Black-and-Grey morality most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T12:06:10-08:00","id":1367827,"title":"","content":"I do not consider it ethically defensible by modern standards, but let's be real here, your sorcerer would have to try pretty hard to be worse than whoever was pushing your new demon around in Malfeas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T13:23:08-08:00","id":1367846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367827#post1367827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not consider it ethically defensible by modern standards, but let's be real here, your sorcerer would have to try pretty hard to be worse than whoever was pushing your new demon around in Malfeas.</div> </div> </div> </div>This leads to a <i>very</i> interesting train of thought. <br /> It's obviously unethical to take a free person and enslave them. But is it ethical to steal a slave and keep them as your slave, provided your treatment of them is less unethical? Do the ethics change if the person is <i>inherently impossible</i> to free and can only exist as a slave? <br /> Various schools of modern morality give different answers! Which means this is a <i>good point of discussion</i>. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T13:50:47-08:00","id":1367852,"title":"","content":"I'm in the 'fails on modern ethics grounds' side of it. Demon summoning where you magically bind them to loyalty, or force them to loyalty through a contest of wills, breaks any non-absurd post-abolitionist worldview of ethical behavior.<br /> <br /> Demon *thaumaturgy* where you just yank them across Cecelyne and then ask them nicely to do things, which they may refuse, no mind-bending involved... is still kidnapping, but is less-bad.<br /> <br /> However, I like to abandon modern ethics at my table, and look at things from the in-universe angle. It helps me storytell the world.<br /> <br /> Exalted is permeated with ethical codes where slavery is often defended and practiced, where all men are not created equal, where the divine right of kings still reigns, where there is a hierarchy of life - even within species, etc. In this time of great (as in terrible) heroes, the slavery of demons is the price of their war reparations. The powers that won the world, and thus those who set the rules, have deemed it just that they may be so ensorcelled, and so it is seen as just. It is a predicate set to bring out the character of the heroes that the players embody - to find the bottom of their character, we give them power (to paraphrase Lincoln).<br /> <br /> Will they choose a civil liberties worldview, that even my worst enemies deserve freedom? Will they literally 'demonize' demons, strip them of humanity, call them the other, and justify their slavery? It is for the player to decide, and for the table to judge them for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:01:10-08:00","id":1367857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367846#post1367846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This leads to a <i>very</i> interesting train of thought. <br /> It's obviously unethical to take a free person and enslave them. But is it ethical to steal a slave and keep them as your slave, provided your treatment of them is less unethical? Do the ethics change if the person is <i>inherently impossible</i> to free and can only exist as a slave? <br /> Various schools of modern morality give different answers! Which means this is a <i>good point of discussion</i>. </div> </div> </div> </div>Even more complex when you realize that some demons aren\u2019t so bad, while others have a natural craving to suck the marrow from human bones. Even if you could grant them their freedom, don\u2019t the innocent people around you deserve not to have a horde of predators unleashed on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:40:44-08:00","id":1367867,"title":"","content":"That begs the question - if you are the demon's jailor, are you responsible for its actions if it goes free? <br /> <br /> I think the core of the question is who is responsible for demon behavior. Does the demon have agency, and thus can take responsibility for its own actions? Then it's the demon's fault. Does the demon have a nature that will override its agency? Then the demon is faultless, it is the demon's master or jailor or bondage-breaker who is to blame. <br /> <br /> Which brings me back to either sharing the definition of humanity with demons (in which case they deserve freedom) or denying them human rights because they are not human (in which case it depends on their nature what it is ethically permissible to allow them, which might justify their indefinite imprisonment.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:44:15-08:00","id":1367870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367852#post1367852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in the 'fails on modern ethics grounds' side of it. Demon summoning where you magically bind them to loyalty, or force them to loyalty through a contest of wills, <b>breaks any non-absurd post-abolitionist worldview of ethical behavior.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree in the strongest terms.<br /> <br /> Demons, by their nature, are not humans.<br /> <br /> Whether rightly or wrongly, the majorty post-abolitionist worldview of ethical behaviour does not extend the same rights and priviliges to non-human animals as it does to humans.<br /> <br /> You can't kidnap a cow and force it into slavery.<br /> <br /> Likewise you cannot kidnap an amphelisiae, and binding one <i>according to most post-abolitionist worldviews of ethical behaviour</i> would be seen as no worse than sending a dog to obediance school.<br /> <br /> I'd certainly argue against according baidak, bisclavarets and luminata the same ethical consideration as humans. They're not people.<br /> <br /> Now whilst a vegan worldview might accord all creatures the same basic dignity of not being chattled into slavery... take at look at tinsiana which <i>literally exist </i>(and I quote) &quot;to dominate and torment the weak&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm quite willing to accept that <i>my own </i>moral code is &quot;absurd&quot;, but I utterly do not accept that there is not <i>any </i>non-absurd view of ethical behaviour that would permit &quot;a contest of wills&quot; to stop a person from &quot;tormenting the weak&quot;.<br /> <br /> Demons are not humans with a funky skin colour and horns.<br /> <br /> They are demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:56:58-08:00","id":1367879,"title":"","content":"Perhaps we could clarify the discussion by using only 2nd circle demons. From what I've read, most of them are, indeed, humans with funky skin colors and horns. But, like, who have really odd parents and were raised under some brutal ideologies.<br /> <br /> They love (Gervesin), they create (Alveua), they talk (except maybe Berengiere?), they trade (Makarios), though there is the odd execption like Sigereth, even Sigereth demonstrates intelligence. Sigereth is like the 'brain in a jar' human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":". 02-14-2020, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:57:05-08:00","id":1367880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367776#post1367776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Puppeteers might ask for babies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Puppeteers don't <i>ask</i> for babies. However, it is just that, if they do <i>find</i> a baby, then they'll <i>try to help</i>. They cannot resist, they <i>must save the babies!</i><br /> <br /> There is not anything sinister or cruel about this; they genuinely want to help and are simply convinced that <i>they know best</i> how to care for a baby.<br /> <br /> They do keep them swaddled, hugged snug and warm in their long tender ribbon arms, and feed them with delicious and nutritious slime. They are not even wrong; the babies are safe and secure, and always <i>want more</i> of the slime \u2026<br /> <br /> ... well, okay, it <i>is</i> highly addictive, but otherwise healthy.<br /> <br /> Anyway, their babies never die from mishandling, malnutrition, or negligence... except ... <i>well</i> \u2026 there is <i>one</i> little issue.<br /> <br /> They do always tend to choke on the puppeteers' nuggetty little bodies in an attempt to suckle more slime. But it is not like the puppeteers want this to happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Puppeteer Bob</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't worry, mate, we're only here to build things. We never interfere with the peoples ...unless the babies are crying.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is it evil to summon puppeteers to build things? If you free them they'll just go find more things to build ... and babies to save.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 02-14-2020, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:13:13-08:00","id":1367888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367879#post1367879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps we could clarify the discussion by using only 2nd circle demons. From what I've read, most of them are, indeed, humans with funky skin colors and horns. But, like, who have really odd parents and were raised under some brutal ideologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, most of them are pretty bad. Like Sigereth gambles with people for their lives, and if they lose the bet she sucks them down to Hell through her little box to become her slave, unless somebody wagers against her to free them. Octavian is a brutal violent warlord who's skin oozes a black oil that poisons the ground around him and anything that touches it, he can't turn it off either. Mara sucks the souls of the living from their mouth with kisses and uses them to fuel her sorcery or other lovers of hers.<br /> <br /> They're more like people in that they tend to have more developed and less animalistic personalities, but they're not <i>nice </i>people, generally. Ted Bundy, Jeffery Dahmer, John Wayne Gacey are all actual human beings but there would still be some practical problems with letting them have their freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:32:48-08:00","id":1367895,"title":"","content":"If I recall 2e at times framed part of the binding check as being able to talk with the demon before it is bound. I recall a mention of blood apes giving token resistance on bindings when they're aware that the task involves doing the whole ripping people apart and drinking the marrow from their bones thing. In which case one could easily use that to be the point where you're laying down your terms and seeing what, if anything, the demon wants in return for their services. Provided of course the demon is sentient, I don't recall much being said about the intelligence of Stomach Bottle Bugs, so binding them to live in you and ingest poisons for a time may be more like when my city handles the wash by roping off an area and dropping off a bunch of goats to graze for the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:02:16-08:00","id":1367902,"title":"","content":"I also don't mean to say that there's no nice demons, or that you might not want to free one from Hell and just let them go because they're actually one of the ones that isn't a terrible predator, but that's on a case-by-case basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:17:02-08:00","id":1367908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367888#post1367888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even then, most of them are pretty bad. [...]<br /> <br /> They're more like people in that they tend to have more developed and less animalistic personalities, but they're not <i>nice </i>people, generally. Ted Bundy, Jeffery Dahmer, John Wayne Gacey are all actual human beings but there would still be some practical problems with letting them have their freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> (I mean... they're all dead so there's not a massive practical problem in letting them have their freedom <i>now</i> but I take your point.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367902#post1367902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't mean to say that there's no nice demons, or that you might not want to free one from Hell and just let them go because they're actually one of the ones that isn't a terrible predator, but that's on a case-by-case basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also agreed.<br /> <br /> Additionally just because I don't advocate giving chimpanzes the same rights as humans, doesn't mean it's ok to torture them either.<br /> <br /> In previous editions neomah existed to trade flesh for flesh. I would argue that binding a neomah to force them to have sex <i>for free </i>would be grossly immoral as this is a violation of their basic nature: &quot;rights are conditions of existence required by man's nature for proper survival&quot;. Binding a neomah that it may trade flesh for flesh, however, would simply be a part of its nature.<br /> <br /> It's cruel to break a song-bird's wings. It's not cruel to enjoy a song-bird's singing, or to build it a bird house in your garden.<br /> <br /> (But now we're firmly into the territory of my own absurd moral code.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-14-2020, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:28:31-08:00","id":1367911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367908#post1367908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I mean... they're all dead so there's not a massive practical problem in letting them have their freedom <i>now</i> but I take your point.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it ethical to permit an evil human to die, knowing that their ghost may commit further evils in the Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:48:24-08:00","id":1367922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367911#post1367911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it ethical to permit an evil human to die, knowing that their ghost may commit further evils in the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming they even leave a ghost. Not everyone who dies remains behind; not everyone who dies <i>can</i> linger as a ghost.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T18:01:24-08:00","id":1367936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367879#post1367879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They love (Gervesin)</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">See, Gervesin loves a guy that he murdered. Between how it's worded and likely sources of inspiration, I've read it for some time as him only having been capable of falling in love with the guy while he was in the process of murdering him. Even in some of the most extreme cases, I'm not sure there's anything quite analogous to the human experience to finding a person lovable while they turn to ash around you.<br /> <br /> I feel as though my perspective on Second Circle Demons is that they can perceive summoning as a frustration unless they're being given something to do that they find very gratifying, but they can put up with it until it's concluded. Maybe even use the opportunity to bring their summoner around on some things.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367880#post1367880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Puppeteers don't <i>ask</i> for babies. However, it is just that, if they do <i>find</i> a baby, then they'll <i>try to help</i>. They cannot resist, they <i>must save the babies!</i><br /> <br /> There is not anything sinister or cruel about this; they genuinely want to help and are simply convinced that <i>they know best</i> how to care for a baby.<br /> <br /> They do keep them swaddled, hugged snug and warm in their long tender ribbon arms, and feed them with delicious and nutritious slime. They are not even wrong; the babies are safe and secure, and always <i>want more</i> of the slime \u2026<br /> <br /> ... well, okay, it <i>is</i> highly addictive, but otherwise healthy.<br /> <br /> Anyway, their babies never die from mishandling, malnutrition, or negligence... except ... <i>well</i> \u2026 there is <i>one</i> little issue.<br /> <br /> They do always tend to choke on the puppeteers' nuggetty little bodies in an attempt to suckle more slime. But it is not like the puppeteers want this to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nnnnnnnnoooo\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A wild puppeteer, freed for some reason to wander the world, often has infants in various states of dehydration and starvation curled up in several non-hopping legs. Puppeteers adore tiny children but have no interest in caring for them. </div> </div> </div>Never gotten an impression that narcotic slime has any nutritional value either. Or that hopping puppeteers can talk.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T18:15:43-08:00","id":1367943,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the puppeteer is not a caregiver; it is a collector.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T22:46:37-08:00","id":1367992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367943#post1367943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the puppeteer is not a caregiver; it is a collector.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh great. Now you remind me of Yugioh. <br /> <br /> On the 'people' and 'abolishment' things.... didn't the laws of the united states state it is for 'persons' not 'humans'? Law might state that it applies for all persons, regardless of species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T23:06:04-08:00","id":1367994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367992#post1367992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh great. Now you remind me of Yugioh.<br /> <br /> On the 'people' and 'abolishment' things.... didn't the laws of the united states state it is for 'persons' not 'humans'? Law might state that it applies for all persons, regardless of species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legality and morality are totally separate though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T23:15:12-08:00","id":1367995,"title":"","content":"So hypothetical, here. You are playing an Exalted Sorceror (lets say Celestial so you can get 2nd Circles at least), and guess what, you're from a progressive (like a weirdo Lunar Clan or a Republican 100 Kingdoms Kingdom) slavery rejecting society and are in fact, all things considered, a pretty decent person.<br /> <br /> Now you got taught Sorcery from a ghost girl who summons flowers, gems, and flowers made out of gems, so she ain't gonna judge, how would you go about making an equitable, as pleasant as possible and non abusive arrangement with:<br /> <br /> 1. A Blood Ape for guard duty (not necessarily any dismemberment involved)<br /> 2. A Neomah, for possibly some mutual enjoyment? Or some other fleshcrafting requirement.<br /> 3. Mara? Cuz black shadow tattoos are the <i>sickest</i>!<br /> 4. Aleuva, because you need help with that daiklaive you're crafting.<br /> <br /> Especially since Step 1 is &quot;rip them away from whatever they were already doing&quot; so you're already in the hole? (Okay, small caveat, you can probably give 5 days notice so they can go through the desert and get there the long way, but is that <i><b>really</b></i> better?)<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-15-2020, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T00:33:06-08:00","id":1368004,"title":"","content":"Well, firstly they may actually be pleased to be brought to Creation because it's not a prison full of demons and titans. It's safer.<br /> <br /> And then, well, you ask.<br /> I suspect of those 4, the Neomah is easiest, the Blood Ape is hardest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T07:01:09-08:00","id":1368036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367995#post1367995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. A Blood Ape for guard duty (not necessarily any dismemberment involved)</div> </div> </div> </div>Poor thing is going to be miserable. At least leave it done cats to snack on.<br /> <br /> At times like this, I think it's worth remembering that task binding is modelled as a Principle. A Defining one to be sure, but that doesn't mean the being is only ever going to do that. I've always pictured blood apes as the kind that can be reasonably patient when expecting prey, but if they're driven stir crazy they're likely to change ranging out beyond the parameters you've set for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. A Neomah, for possibly some mutual enjoyment? Or some other fleshcrafting requirement.<br /> 3. Mara? Cuz black shadow tattoos are the <i>sickest</i>!</div> </div> </div> </div>Neomah are a kind I think are generally enthusiastic about the possibilities of most things a summoner would call them for. Mind, Masters of Jade did have a Guildmember use some to create some beacons and then abandon them there, so that's definitely a misuse.<br /> <br /> Displaying any dark proclivities around Mara is the kind of thing that could very well get her returning of her own accord to explore what you're made of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Okay, small caveat, you can probably give 5 days notice so they can go through the desert and get there the long way, but is that <i><b>really</b></i> better?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the past when summoning has been described from the perspective of a demon, spending five days crossing Cecylene was the default. They just got the call five days before you made it so they could arrive on time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T07:07:33-08:00","id":1368038,"title":"","content":"But how would you model it in game? Do the ritual and instead of the willpower-off for a binding you say, &quot;Terribly sorry to interrupt your hellish routine, but I've got a task that needs helping with, and I'm sure we can arrange some quid pro quo?&quot; and try to social action bargain them into it instead?<br /> <br /> Because the danger there is that they straight up lie to you and run off to wreak havoc once you're not looking.<br /> <br /> I suppose it depends on the demon and if you successfully leverage it's love of cats to get it to do what you want.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-15-2020, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T07:49:59-08:00","id":1368043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1368038#post1368038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the danger there is that they straight up lie to you and run off to wreak havoc once you're not looking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prototype, that's not how the social system works. If you successfully influence someone, they are committed to taking action and you the player are aware of this. If their Resolve is higher but they <i>act</i> like they were persuaded, you the player are aware of this, and can take Read Intentions/Socialize Charms/Judge's Ear Technique to realize in-character whether they seem genuine. If you successfully influence someone and they invoke a Decision Point, but they act like they were persuaded, you the player are <i>still</i> aware of this, and those same options exist to see how genuine they are.<br /> <br /> \u200bAbout the only way they can just change their mind afterward - and you the player not know about it - is if someone overturns your influence off-screen, or other circumstances are introduced. And it would be poor STing if the ST didn't at least foreshadow that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-15-2020, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T08:01:19-08:00","id":1368046,"title":"","content":"My mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-15-2020, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T08:23:08-08:00","id":1368048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1368043#post1368043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prototype, that's not how the social system works. If you successfully influence someone, they are committed to taking action and you the player are aware of this. If their Resolve is higher but they <i>act</i> like they were persuaded, you the player are aware of this, and can take Read Intentions/Socialize Charms/Judge's Ear Technique to realize in-character whether they seem genuine. If you successfully influence someone and they invoke a Decision Point, but they act like they were persuaded, you the player are <i>still</i> aware of this, and those same options exist to see how genuine they are.<br /> <br /> \u200bAbout the only way they can just change their mind afterward - and you the player not know about it - is if someone overturns your influence off-screen, or other circumstances are introduced. And it would be poor STing if the ST didn't at least foreshadow that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quite aware of how the social system works, I am positing a state of affairs where:<br /> <br /> 1. You do not successfully persuade said demon.<br /> <br /> 2. Said demon acts like they were persuaded.<br /> <br /> 3. You are unable to successfully penetrate their guile (either lacking the items you mentioned or just being poor at it)<br /> <br /> 4. They lie to the character and say they are their willing servant and are sent off to ostensibly do the summoner's will.<br /> <br /> Sure, at this point you the player knows that the demon is lying their ass off, but the character would not (barring charms and whatnot), and I try not to bring a whole bunch of metagaming into this, so it would behoove said character to act like they believe the lie, because they do.<br /> <br /> Then, mass murder is entirely possible on the demons side, because they lied and got away with it. Whereas with the Willpower binding, this isn't a danger.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-15-2020, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T08:40:14-08:00","id":1368049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics#post1367763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but that sounds like a lot of the apologism for slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to struggle to find a way to present non-humans that hasn't been used by racists to say why another group of humans is untrustworthy or deserving of subjugation. The trick is to know and listen to your intended audiance and shut out the people looking for a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T09:40:24-08:00","id":1368053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1368048#post1368048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Then, mass murder is entirely possible on the demons side, because they lied and got away with it. Whereas with the Willpower binding, this isn't a danger.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, accepting the possibility of being deceived and betrayed is a necessary component of all relationships founded on trust rather than systems of control. That's the price one pays for not wanting to subjugate people.<br /> <br /> That being said, an unbound neomah isn't a danger to anybody except possibly the baby they'll abandon. Or a stomach bottle bug. There are plenty of demons one can go with that don't go on murderous rampages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T10:46:14-08:00","id":1368065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics#post1367763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the question is, is in the face of modern ethics, is it in any way defensible to summon, and bind, demons and elementals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on which ethical framework you're using. From a Kantian framework, if you consider the demon a sapient person, it's unethical to treat the demon as a means rather than an end. From a virtue ethics framework, it'd depend on what you had the demon do and why--laziness and greed aren't particularly virtuous, but courage and civic duty might be. A divine command ethical framework would depend a lot on what your god, faith, or guiding philosophy thinks of demons--they don't have souls, for instance, and some faiths would dismiss their personhood as a result. From a utilitarian standpoint, demon-summoning might create more happiness and better outcomes, even for the demon. That said, many demons aren't particularly comfortable in Creation, and might not agree with human definitions of kind treatment.<br /> <br /> If your ethical framework prioritizes self-determination for sapient beings as a good, then demon-summoning is unethical. Given that it automatically involves binding in Ex3, demon-summoning in such a framework is unethical even if the demon agrees to it ahead of time, because they effectively lose any free will about their bound task. No amount of advance buy-in balances the removal of that capacity for a year or more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1367771#post1367771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. But here's the thing: if it wanted to do that stuff anyway, then all you've really done is given it a free ticket to Creation and asked it to do that on your behalf specifically. Heck, you can even pay the demon for its labor; the spell isn't stopping you from doing so.<br /> (...)<br /> And in the wrong hands, demon summoning is absolutely slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div>If one binds the demon's will (and the sorcerer is required to try), then it's slavery regardless of what one binds the demon to do. The term &quot;slave&quot; is used in the spell's description for a reason. The question is thus whether enslavement of demons--who are inhuman, alien, and already enslaved for life by greater demons--is wrong. If sapience and/or sentience are the measures of ethical worth, then demon-binding is basically just exploiting a contract with another slaver to use their slave for an agreed-upon period of time, then forcing the slave to go along with the contract.<br /> <br /> A demon's lot is oppression due to the nature of Hell and the oaths extracted by the Exalted long ago, but that doesn't mean they like it. In fact, we know that demons usually resent a failed binding attempt because the spell tells us so. A successful binding simply removes the demon's ability to resent it, which is a far cry from allowing the demon agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T20:04:24-08:00","id":1368211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1368065#post1368065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your ethical framework prioritizes self-determination for sapient beings as a good, then demon-summoning is unethical.</div> </div> </div> </div>This about sums up my out-of-game position on the question. Well put.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T02:18:21-08:00","id":1368257,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=ZerUbHmuY04\" target=\"_blank\">Remind me how we're defining &quot;sapient&quot; this week?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T03:28:44-08:00","id":1368274,"title":"","content":"My demon summoning Twilight crafter has the Defining Intimacy &quot;It is acceptable to use Malfean Resources&quot; and the Major intimacy &quot;1st circle demons are things, not people&quot;. His limited trigger is suffering shame or being scolded for using demons. Its a hot button for him. He sees them as barely sentient beings of alien mind which are constantly forming and dissolving into the make-up of Malfeas itself, so it doesn't matter what he does with them. <br /> <br /> So yeah, classic slavery. <br /> <br /> He also has a custom artifact which lets him smelt demons/elementals into artifact weapons so he <i>literally</i> uses them as things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T03:42:50-08:00","id":1368277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1368274#post1368274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My demon summoning Twilight crafter has the Defining Intimacy &amp;quot;It is acceptable to use Malfean Resources&amp;quot; and the Major intimacy &amp;quot;1st circle demons are things, not people&amp;quot;. His limited trigger is suffering shame or being scolded for using demons. Its a hot button for him. He sees them as barely sentient beings of alien mind which are constantly forming and dissolving into the make-up of Malfeas itself, so it doesn't matter what he does with them. <br /> <br /> So yeah, classic slavery. <br /> <br /> He also has a custom artifact which lets him smelt demons/elementals into artifact weapons so he <i>literally</i> uses them as things.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many times has he been scolded or shamed for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T05:47:16-08:00","id":1368288,"title":"","content":"I'm currently the ST, so almost never. I couldn't think of a better word for scolded (i am in the middle of a MASSIVE headcold atm). The actual wording is ... I can't remember right now. Anytime people question his methods about using demons or deny his help because of the demons or start to question the demon thing he gets pretty table flippy. For a one shot I got to play he was told he couldn't bring any demons into the city and he almost got assassinated because he was alone in his workshop. <br /> <br /> His character design is built around turning demons into malfean brass* and turning that into artifacts, so he has a very, very severe reaction to people questioning his methods. He also learned Craft under Alveua, and he inherited some of her apathy towards using living beings as a craft resource. <br /> <br /> *His Artifact anvil has an evocation called 'Shortcuts Through Hell'. Take that, Devs!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T21:21:45-08:00","id":1368677,"title":"","content":"I find myself thinking that it should be possible to engage with a relationship between a sorcerer and demon in a manner reminiscent of the story of Ali Baba and Morgiana.<br /> <br /> Mindful of the likelihood that the story is probably a tad idealised, if not deeply riddled with bias to the point of being propaganda, but it's still compelling and reflects a dynamic that could arise between people and their closest (and most skilled) slaves.<br /> <br /> Even at larger, more impersonal scales, there's a range between the slave of plantation or mine, and the one appointed to high military and administrative positions and engaged in rituals of elaborate gift giving. None of that is particularly good, but some of them can have complexities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T00:11:25-08:00","id":1368694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1368677#post1368677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find myself thinking that it should be possible to engage with a relationship between a sorcerer and demon in a manner reminiscent of the story of Ali Baba and Morgiana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though hopefully without the demon walking in on the sorcerer &quot;checking his wounds.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T10:44:21-08:00","id":1368770,"title":"","content":"What if demon summoning is like medieval feudalism (of which I have a very limited, mostly wikipedia based understanding). <br /> <br /> The Yozi are effectively vassals of the Exalted host, serving them in exchange for their own little fiefdom in Hell. In exchange, (admittedly just 'not killing the Yozi' rather than protecting the Yozi) they offer serviceas vassals, sending their tenants, the demons to summoners as payment in kind for their vassal status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T15:04:03-08:00","id":1368803,"title":"","content":"I think that it's not really fair to describe the Yozis as having been &quot;given&quot; lands, since they're imprisoned within themselves. They live in themselves, mutilated, not some nice land the Solars gave them.<br /> <br /> But I could definitely see a PC <i>thinking</i> of it that way, especially if they come from a culture with something like that.<br /> <br /> (On Feudalism... yeah, that's kind of right. If you ask Medieval historians these days, they'll mostly say &quot;There's no such thing as feudalism!&quot; By which they mean there was no all-encompassing system across Europe, it was very ad-hoc, full of exceptions and different rules, and complications. But in 12th and 13th century England, the closest thing to Feudalism, yeah, each Lord owed the King the military service of X soldiers, depending on how much land they had, for X time a year, generally 40 days. Lords became very unhappy if they had to come fight for more than 40 days. It became more and more common to just pay the King scuttage: some money in lieu of sending soldiers. Scuttage became more standardised over time, until by the 16th century Lords were just paying a standardised war tax based on how much land they had. Then the King would hire soldiers for that war with the money.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-18-2020, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T17:45:10-08:00","id":1368827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1368803#post1368803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">each Lord owed the King the military service of X soldiers, depending on how much land they had, for X time a year, generally 40 days. </div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes an obligation to several different kings. Got a bit awkward if those obligations were ever incompatible (not just service owed to warring kings, sometimes serving one in campaign took you away from being available for another). It's just like that episode of... well, everything.<br /> <br /> The Demon of the First Circle spell... I'm uncomfortable speculating on its intent while the writer is right there, nor do I want to interrogate Vance about it. Suffice to say that for me personally, some of its language reads as necessary shorthand to get the essential points across, which maybe does require a bit of reflection as one sees more and more demons. That and it's a big deal how binding is modelled, which I think is worth focusing on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T19:47:20-08:00","id":1369087,"title":"","content":"Something I'm curious about is whether we're going to see a return of Limit tracks and Templates for Time-bound demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25940-arykaran","name":"ArykAran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25940_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T02:32:34-08:00","id":1369117,"title":"","content":"I think it's unlikely, though personally I quite liked it.<br /> Still, they've actually reduced your control this edition; bound demons have a Defining Intimacy to follow your orders, but that's no stronger than their other Defining Intimacy(/ies). So there's going to be some issues there if you give them the wrong orders anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T14:39:00-08:00","id":1369206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArykAran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1369087#post1369087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'm curious about is whether we're going to see a return of Limit tracks and Templates for Time-bound demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't expect it. The Abcissic templates were cool, but involved way more complexity and book-keeping than they were worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T18:08:25-08:00","id":1369256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1367763-on-demon-summoning-and-ethics?p=1369206#post1369206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't expect it. The Abcissic templates were cool, but involved way more complexity and book-keeping than they were worth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This makes me incredibly happy. I am glad we won't have a third &quot;overturn how the spell works in corebook for this sorcery rules&quot; incident.First Ed, forgivable, given the evolution. Going from that back to &quot;Same as first ed core&quot; for 2nd ed core, then back to &quot;basically same as savant and sorcerer&quot; with the roll of glorious divinity felt unrefined. Since the leaning is that &quot;it's a defining intimacy and it'll stay that way&quot; just feels better. At least to me.<br /> <br /> Not saying I didn't see benefit in the Abcissic templates, but if they're going to be kept, promote them to core. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25940-arykaran","name":"ArykAran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25940_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}